// # sec/cap — Capability Tokens
//
// Logline: The capability token system (Pillar 5). 20 implemented tokens including Bind and CompilerRead. 6 future-state reserved (Audio, Camera, Usb, Hid, Window, Frame). Token derivation uses getentropy(3) — fail-closed (no LCG fallback). Rule 2 HMAC is MAC-bound. Path caps use directory boundaries.
//
//
// Setup: Domain module. Caps and layout are in the parent ANCHOR.oo.
// Beats:
//   1. caps.h — the OODAR_CAP_* bit-layout and the 19 implemented + 7 reserved token kinds.
//   2. caps.c — orchestrator: the getentropy-derived token creation and attestation; the 22-token canonical store.
//   3. cap.c — seal, eq, plus the seccomp-bpf filter application.
//   4. cap_grant.c — the 22 oo_cap_grant_* primitives (the canonical grant surface).
//   5. cap_require.c — oo_cap_require_* family (the per-cap predicates used by every public mutator).
//   6. cap_attenuate_path.c — oo_attenuate_fsread_to_path + oo_path_cap_check (OoPathCap with path prefix).
//   7. cap_attenuate_hmac.c — oo_cap_attenuate / oo_cap_attenuate_v2 (HMAC-sealed; v2 enforces Rule 2).
//   8. cap_alloc.c — AllocCap subsystem (moved from core/mem/alloc.c in v3.4.0 per the round-6 audit).
//   9. cap_time.c — TimeCap / RandCap subsystem (moved from fs/os/time_rand.c in v3.4.0).
//  10. cap_ffi.c — FFICap subsystem (moved from app/xlang/ffi_sec.c in v3.4.0).
//
// v2.3.0 file split: the original 428-line caps.c was split into
// caps.c (orchestrator) + cap_grant.c + cap_require.c + cap_attenuate.c.
// The split is functional (one cap-primitive per file). The shared
// state (g_tok_*, g_seal_key, g_kernel_hmac_key) lives in caps.c and
// is exposed as extern to the satellite files.
//
// v3.1.0 audit cleanup: removed cap_seal.c (the oo_cap_kernel_seal /
// oo_enclave_enter primitives had 0 callers in the umbrella; the
// sealed-cap surface is provided by app/actor/actor_rpc.c and
// sec/crypto/seal.c).
//
// v3.4.0 round-6 cleanup: cap_attenuate.c split into cap_attenuate_path.c
// (path-cap) + cap_attenuate_hmac.c (HMAC seal, formerly lived in
// sec/crypto/symmetric/crypto.c — layering-inversion fix). cap_alloc.c
// + cap_time.c + cap_ffi.c created to host the cap stores that lived
// in the wrong directories per the round-6 misplaced-files audit.
//
// ──▓▓ sec/cap ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Pillar 5 — unforgeable, kernel-derived ::
